n** = the canary re-runs the same child on the same input and compares a SHA-256 of canonical (sorted-key, exact-number) stdout. Artifact = `{claim_id, domain, nonce, stdout_hash, exit_code, runtime_fingerprint}` where runtime_fingerprint = `{node_major, canonicalization_version}` (reproduced or recorded so a version skew is detected, not silently hashed-around).\n- **Inherited modules:** resolved via a pinned **`inherits.manifest.json`** (repo root) mapping each logical name â†’ resolvable path + expected exports (Phase-0 handoff/journal/sleep; Gandalf v1 commission seam; the three dive engines). The Wave-2 A0.5a gate reads it and fails fast on any unresolvable/mismatched entry. Authoring the manifest is the first deliverable of Wave 2 (its terminus-acceptance artifact).\n\n## Â§Residuals â€” REQUIRED-BEFORE-BUILD, PINNED (value Â· owner Â· terminus-acceptance)\n- **A0.5a (inheritance gate)** â€” *value:* `inherits.manifest.json` + a `node --test` resolving/version/interface-shape-checking each entry. *Owner:* Wave 2. *Terminus:* green test; fails fast on any unresolvable/mismatched entry.\n- **R1 (oracle roster + per-class k + kâ€² + FP tolerance)** â€” *value:* 6 planted-defect classes (derivation-error, dimensional, off-by-one, convergence-stability, comprehension-narrative, firewall-inapplicable) Ã— â‰¥3 instances; a FIXED **6-fixture SOUND subset** (separate from the iâ€“xiv union, used ONLY for the false-positive / kâ€² term and EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator); per-class catch floors: **derivation/dimensional/off-by-one = 100%**, **convergence-stability/comprehension-narrative/firewall-inapplicable â‰¥ 2/3 each**; **kâ€² = at most 1 false positive on the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset** (absolute integer). *kâ€² and the Metric-G false-positive-rate intentionally share the SOUND-subset cardinality (kâ€² = count form, G FP-rate = rate form of the same observations), so that cardinality is a single load-bearing constant.* Numeric-anchor FP tolerance = relative 1e-9. *Owner:* Wave 24 (corpus) + Wave 25 (scoring). *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when asserts all per-class floors + kâ€².\n- **Metric G + canned baseline (the oracle gate)** â€” *value:* **G = catch-rate âˆ’ false-positive-rate** over the canonical **SCORED SUBSET** (= the planted-defect computational/firewall fixtures; the FIXED 6-fixture SOUND subset is EXCLUDED from the catch-rate denominator and feeds only the FP/kâ€² term â€” the SAME token is used verbatim in the Wave-25 done-when). The canned baseline is PINNED as TWO stub scorers â€” **always-ABSTAIN** and **always-FLAG** â€” scored on the identical SCORED SUBSET with G computed by the identical formula; **acceptance = G(battery-on) > G(better stub) + 0.30 (strict)** AND the ablation arm scores measurably lower; **ABSTAIN-correctness floor = 100%** of proof/conceptual arms ABSTAIN. *Owner:* Wave 25. *Terminus:* the Wave-25 done-when cites the SCORED SUBSET token, the two stub baselines, the 0.30 epsilon, the per-class floors, kâ€², and the 100% abstain floor.\n- **S1 (CONTROL thresholds + gap-function)** â€” *value:* budget = 8 steps; gap-function = no progress-boolean=true in the last m=3 steps â‡’ switch; 2 consecutive switches â‡’ ABANDON; on the pinned canned non-converging fixture ABANDON fires via the gap-function **strictly before step 8** (reason=gap-function, never budget-exhausted). *Owner:* Wave 17. *Terminus:* the ABANDON fixture exits reason=gap-function before step 8, claim left UNVERIFIED.\n- **S4 (ref-fn-independence invariant)** â€” *value:* a firewall ref-fn whose AST shares no symbol-provenance with the comprehension narrative; else cap at CLAIMED. *Owner:* Wave 11. *Terminus:* the planted-wrong-same-family-reference fixture caps at CLAIMED.\n- **P3 (example-space-stability predicate)** â€” *value:* ADVISORY-only; \"stable\" = no new monster in the last r=2 example-rounds; never gates promotion. *Owner:* Wave 20. *Terminus:* a forged-but-unfaithful but example-stable definition still stamps requires-Phase-F.\n- **P7 (default-deny grammar + battery + recall roster + closure)** â€” *value:* a CLOSED whitelist grammar over EXACT arithmetic (numeric literals; finite arithmetic ops; bounded finite sums/products with literal bounds; NO float/symbolic/unbounded/quantified nodes); â‰¥8 positive-recall computations (incl. â‰¥1 nested-composition) it MUST settle; â‰¥8 smuggled-non-literal inputs (incl. â‰¥1 deep-nested-smuggle) it MUST reject. *Owner:* Wave 8 (grammar+battery) + Wave 9 (recall) + Waves 24/25 (scored). *Terminus:* 100% reject on the battery AND 100% settle on the recall roster, closure-tested.\n- **P9 (provenance-binding contract)** â€” *value:* artifact = `{claim_id, domain, nonce, stdout_hash, exit_code, runtime_fingerprint}` from the Wave-9 subprocess [/ .olean / SMT cert in Increment-2]; canary re-execution = re-run the subprocess and compare the SHA-256 stdout hash; freshness = a **single-use claim-bound nonce = hash(claim_id + domain + monotone-counter)** where the monotone-counter is **DURABLE + monotone across restarts** (last-issued value per (claim_id,domain) persisted to the Phase-0 durability substrate â€” reuse, no new store; acceptable alt: a high-entropy per-mint random nonce + a persisted spent-nonce set the canary checks). **Write-ordering:** the counter-persist (or spent-nonce record) is ordered-BEFORE the artifact becomes valid, so a crash after mint but before flush leaves no usable replayable nonce on restart. Wave 2 round-trips the durable counter/spent-set across a simulated reload before Wave 4 relies on it. *Owner:* Wave 4 (+ Wave 2 substrate round-trip, Wave 6, Waves 24/25). *Terminus:* the E1 forged-artifact, cross-claim-replay, same-claim-replay, across-restart-replay, AND crash-mid-mint attempts are all rejected.\n- **P8 (SMT/cross-family integrity)** â€” *Increment-2 (Phase F).* *Value:* probabilistic-class integrity = N=5 trials at temp=0; pass-threshold = 5/5 reject of a known-FALSE sentinel + 5/5 accept